# Byte-exact policy for artifacts whose SHA-256 is asserted in a committed record.
#
# Everything not listed here keeps Git's default handling. These paths are
# different: a committed artifact records their SHA-256, so any line-ending
# rewrite on checkout invalidates a published hash. '-text' disables end-of-line
# conversion entirely, in both directions, so the working tree always holds the
# same bytes as the blob on every platform.
#
# Why this was needed: before this file existed, cloning on Windows with the
# Git-for-Windows default core.autocrlf=true rewrote these files and
# scripts/reproduce.py exited 1 at stage 2 (frozen manifest) and failed the
# register_sha256 comparison at stage 4. The repository verified only on the
# machine that produced it.

# Register whose SHA-256 is recorded as register_sha256 in
# gates/results/GATE_19_EXTERNAL_AUDIT.json (harness stage 4).
gates/baselines/GATE_19_EXTERNAL_MCP_PAIRS.json -text

